  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 236 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nUpper trough continues to push through the eastern Plains and\nwill be moving off into the Great Lakes tonight. Behind the\ntrough, northwesterly flow aloft sets up for most of the period\nas ridging continues over the Four Corners region. Northwesterly\nflow aloft continues into the upcoming work week, with most of\nthe shortwaves producing precipitation staying north in Canada.\nUpper heights trend upwards a bit towards the end of the week,\nwith some of the ensemble members bringing the ridging east and\nthen setting up southwesterly flow aloft over the weekend. \nOther clusters of ensemble members have ridging right over us or\nnorthwesterly flow continuing. Confidence in dry and mild\npattern is high through at least Thursday, then decreases for\ndays 6 and 7.\n\n...Rain ending and warm and dry pattern setting in...\n\nBand of light rain currently over west central MN is associated\nwith some mid-level frontogenesis, and is expected to move east\nout of our area in the next three hours. Drier air setting in\nbehind the band, and think northwesterly winds will keep any fog\ntonight at bay even with recent rainfall. Northwesterly flow\naloft continues into the upcoming week, with probabilities of at\nleast a 0.01 of rain near zero except for some 10 percents near\nLake of the Woods towards the end of the week. ECWMF EFI shows a\ntrend towards temps above seasonal averages, but nothing on the\nextreme end of climo at this point.",
